WEBVTT

NOTE Work Injury or Illness — CFHR training, current as of 11.09.2026. Built from the narration manifest by scripts/build-vtt.mjs.

1
00:00:07.235 --> 00:00:10.200
This is manager training on California work injury

2
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:14.223
and illness, current as of November 9th, 2026.

3
00:00:14.223 --> 00:00:16.849
It's a framework, not legal advice.

4
00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:20.085
Monday morning, your employee is hurt on the job.

5
00:00:20.085 --> 00:00:21.467
Maybe he's back Wednesday;

6
00:00:21.467 --> 00:00:22.930
maybe it's months.

7
00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:25.083
Two questions decide everything:

8
00:00:25.083 --> 00:00:26.546
is his job protected,

9
00:00:26.546 --> 00:00:28.473
and is anything replacing his pay?

10
00:00:28.496 --> 00:00:30.893
For a work injury the answers flip.

11
00:00:30.893 --> 00:00:32.234
The pay is owed at every

12
00:00:32.234 --> 00:00:34.470
employer, through your own insurance.

13
00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:36.542
The job has no leave law of its own.

14
00:00:36.542 --> 00:00:38.594
The first clock is yours.

15
00:00:40.885 --> 00:00:43.282
He's told to report it within thirty days.

16
00:00:43.282 --> 00:00:44.542
Don't count his days:

17
00:00:44.542 --> 00:00:46.167
the moment you know, from him

18
00:00:46.167 --> 00:00:48.630
or from anyone, your clock starts.

19
00:00:48.695 --> 00:00:50.727
If he loses time beyond his shift,

20
00:00:50.727 --> 00:00:53.490
or needs treatment beyond first aid, hand him

21
00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:57.944
the claim form, the DWC 1, within one working day.

22
00:00:57.995 --> 00:00:59.010
If it's serious:

23
00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:03.521
inpatient hospitalization, amputation, loss of an eye, serious

24
00:01:03.521 --> 00:01:07.787
permanent disfigurement, or death, Cal/OSHA hears from you

25
00:01:07.787 --> 00:01:10.104
immediately, and no later than eight hours

26
00:01:10.104 --> 00:01:12.314
after you knew, or should have known.

27
00:01:12.362 --> 00:01:15.166
Your own report, Form 5020, goes

28
00:01:15.166 --> 00:01:17.720
to your insurer within five days.

29
00:01:20.465 --> 00:01:22.171
The pay first, because it comes

30
00:01:22.171 --> 00:01:24.488
from one place at every employer:

31
00:01:24.488 --> 00:01:27.048
workers' comp temporary disability, through your

32
00:01:27.048 --> 00:01:30.388
insurance, not State Disability Insurance.

33
00:01:30.456 --> 00:01:33.260
It pays two-thirds of his average weekly wage:

34
00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:35.291
for injuries in 2026, from

35
00:01:35.291 --> 00:01:41.485
$264.61 to $1,764.11 a week.

36
00:01:41.598 --> 00:01:44.077
The first three days are unpaid, unless he's admitted

37
00:01:44.077 --> 00:01:46.637
to the hospital or off more than fourteen days;

38
00:01:46.637 --> 00:01:47.970
then they're paid back.

39
00:01:48.036 --> 00:01:50.149
The first payment, or a delay notice,

40
00:01:50.149 --> 00:01:51.815
is due within fourteen days of your

41
00:01:51.815 --> 00:01:53.888
knowing he's hurt and off work.

42
00:01:53.888 --> 00:01:55.878
Then every two weeks, up to one

43
00:01:55.878 --> 00:01:58.431
hundred four weeks within five years.

44
00:02:01.235 --> 00:02:03.510
When the form comes back, two things happen

45
00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:05.586
on your side within one working day:

46
00:02:05.586 --> 00:02:07.983
he and the claims administrator each get

47
00:02:07.983 --> 00:02:09.771
a dated copy with your section filled

48
00:02:09.771 --> 00:02:13.388
in, and treatment is authorized, up to $10,000,

49
00:02:13.388 --> 00:02:16.194
until the claim is accepted or denied.

50
00:02:16.255 --> 00:02:18.489
If the claim can't be decided yet, he hears

51
00:02:18.489 --> 00:02:21.090
that in writing within the same fourteen days.

52
00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:23.366
And within ninety days of the claim form,

53
00:02:23.366 --> 00:02:25.032
it's accepted or denied,

54
00:02:25.032 --> 00:02:27.537
or the claim is presumed compensable.

55
00:02:30.015 --> 00:02:31.152
Now the job.

56
00:02:31.152 --> 00:02:33.021
There's no work-injury leave law.

57
00:02:33.021 --> 00:02:35.581
Instead, three protections at once.

58
00:02:35.581 --> 00:02:36.232
One:

59
00:02:36.232 --> 00:02:41.011
Labor Code section 132a, at every employer, throughout.

60
00:02:41.065 --> 00:02:42.689
You can't punish or fire him

61
00:02:42.689 --> 00:02:44.925
for the injury, for filing the claim,

62
00:02:44.925 --> 00:02:47.759
or for testifying in a co-worker's case.

63
00:02:47.789 --> 00:02:48.399
Two:

64
00:02:48.399 --> 00:02:51.244
if the injury is also a serious health condition,

65
00:02:51.244 --> 00:02:53.031
and he has twelve months of service

66
00:02:53.031 --> 00:02:55.916
and twelve hundred fifty hours in the past year,

67
00:02:55.916 --> 00:02:58.802
CFRA holds the job for up to twelve

68
00:02:58.802 --> 00:03:02.686
weeks at five or more employees, with FMLA

69
00:03:02.686 --> 00:03:06.693
alongside at fifty or more within seventy-five miles.

70
00:03:06.769 --> 00:03:10.020
Designate it in writing within five business days, so

71
00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:12.370
the twelve weeks run with the comp leave.

72
00:03:12.438 --> 00:03:13.169
Three:

73
00:03:13.169 --> 00:03:18.573
California's disability law, FEHA, at five or more employees:

74
00:03:18.573 --> 00:03:21.377
accommodation and the interactive process, with no

75
00:03:21.377 --> 00:03:23.799
fixed end date, case by case.

76
00:03:27.075 --> 00:03:28.497
Look at week twelve.

77
00:03:28.497 --> 00:03:33.495
CFRA and FMLA end here, if they applied

78
00:03:33.495 --> 00:03:35.526
and you designated them from the start.

79
00:03:35.526 --> 00:03:37.071
Nothing else does.

80
00:03:37.132 --> 00:03:39.692
Temporary disability follows the medical evidence,

81
00:03:39.692 --> 00:03:41.601
up to one hundred four weeks.

82
00:03:41.601 --> 00:03:44.608
Section 132a doesn't end at week twelve,

83
00:03:44.608 --> 00:03:46.459
and it doesn't end with the claim.

84
00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:49.436
The duty to accommodate has no fixed end.

85
00:03:49.436 --> 00:03:51.386
So the trigger here isn't a date;

86
00:03:51.386 --> 00:03:52.767
it's a restriction.

87
00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:54.474
The day his doctor sends him back with

88
00:03:54.474 --> 00:03:57.661
a work restriction, the interactive process starts.

89
00:03:57.675 --> 00:03:59.301
Run it alongside the claim,

90
00:03:59.301 --> 00:04:01.055
not after the claim closes.

91
00:04:04.735 --> 00:04:06.320
So the bottom line.

92
00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:07.335
The pay:

93
00:04:07.335 --> 00:04:09.001
two-thirds of his wages, through

94
00:04:09.001 --> 00:04:11.507
your insurance, at every employer.

95
00:04:11.579 --> 00:04:13.773
The job is protected three ways at once:

96
00:04:13.773 --> 00:04:16.170
no retaliation throughout, up to twelve weeks

97
00:04:16.170 --> 00:04:18.284
of CFRA and FMLA if

98
00:04:18.284 --> 00:04:21.602
it qualifies, accommodation with no fixed end.

99
00:04:21.702 --> 00:04:23.613
The fastest clocks here are yours:

100
00:04:23.613 --> 00:04:25.807
eight hours for a serious injury,

101
00:04:25.807 --> 00:04:28.435
and one working day for the claim form.

102
00:04:28.506 --> 00:04:30.253
A work restriction is the start

103
00:04:30.253 --> 00:04:33.620
of the accommodation conversation, not something to wait out.
